{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607070800-net-babiniku-llm-backend-claude-sonnet-5"
  :title "ADR-2607070800: net-babiniku LLM chat backend -- Claude Sonnet 5, structured
          outputs, no self-fine-tune"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "net-babiniku-llm-backend"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-07"
  :authoritative_for
  ["net-babiniku's SFW chat tier uses a hosted Claude Sonnet 5 call, not a self-fine-tuned/
    self-hosted model -- club-shinshi's uncensored-model precedent does not apply to this tier"
   "the Anthropic API call lives only in a Cloudflare Pages Function (functions/api/chat.js),
    never in browser-shipped .cljs -- the API key must never reach client code"
   "every chat turn's shape is enforced via Claude structured outputs (output_config.format),
    with emotion/motion_cue enums drawn directly from babiniku.governor/default-policy -- a
    schema-conformant reply can only ever fail review-turn on content, never on shape"
   "the fetched turn always routes through babiniku.governor/review-turn via :governor/propose
    -- the same gate every pre-existing demo button used; nothing about this feature is a new
    bypass path"
   "if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is unprovisioned, the Function returns 503 -- never a crash, never a
    fabricated turn (honest-default, ADR-0084 pattern)"]
  :related
  ["90-docs/adr/2607062200-net-babiniku-onlyfans-style-creator-monetization.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607062210-net-babiniku-giemon-humanoid-embodiment-procurement.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607062300-jk-luxury-org-club-shinshi-net-babiniku-relocation.md"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "user direction 2026-07-06/07: pivot to big decisions needing user input,
           specifically LLM backend selection -- 'shinshi.clubの前例（自家fine-tune+Modal/
           vLLM）を踏襲するか、別のアプローチか。' User chose Claude Sonnet 5 as the model
           tier, and chose to implement now."
  :prior_state
  {:what "net-babiniku had reached Milestone 2 (governor HARD/SOFT containment, monetization
          honest-default, giemon embodiment gate) with NO real chat feature -- every dialogue
          'proposal' was a hardcoded demo button (db/default-db's :demo-proposals). No LLM
          provider/model had ever been chosen."}
  :club_shinshi_precedent
  {:what "club-shinshi (separate jk-luxury product, now owned by a different agent) self-
          fine-tunes + self-hosts (Modal/vLLM, ADR-2606032100) an uncensored model because its
          paid tier includes NSFW roleplay a hosted API's classifiers would refuse"
   :why_it_does_not_apply "net-babiniku's chat feature per this ADR is SFW-only -- the still-
                          open content-rating decision (ADR-2607062200's paid tier 'may
                          include NSFW') is untouched and out of scope here. For SFW-only
                          chat, a hosted model with a good system prompt is sufficient; self-
                          hosting buys nothing this tier needs."}
  :model_tiers_considered
  {:haiku_4_5 {:price "$1/$5 per MTok" :pros "fastest, cheapest, cost/latency-optimal default"
               :caveats "min cacheable prompt is 4096 tokens (a terse persona prompt wouldn't
                        clear it); roleplay/persona consistency is a plausible weak point for
                        a VTuber product"}
   :sonnet_5 {:price "$3/$15 per MTok ($2/$10 intro through 2026-08-31)"
              :why_chosen "user's choice -- meaningfully better roleplay/persona consistency,
                          cost/latency premium judged acceptable at this feature's current
                          scale; supports structured outputs the same as Haiku 4.5 would"}
   :opus_tier {:considered? false
               :why "this is a low-cost real-time chat-turn workload, not a code-authorship
                    task where the claude-api skill's default-to-Opus guidance applies -- user
                    was asked to choose directly between the two cost-appropriate tiers"}}}

 :decision
 {:model {:what "claude-sonnet-5" :self_fine_tune? false :self_hosted? false}
  :structured_outputs
  {:what "every chat turn request sets output_config.format to a json_schema constraining the
          reply to {dialogue, emotion, motion_cue}, with emotion/motion_cue enums drawn
          directly from babiniku.governor/default-policy's :allowed-emotions/
          :allowed-motion-cues -- not a separately maintained list"
   :why "a schema-conformant reply can only ever fail review-turn on CONTENT (a blocked term,
        an ambiguous content-tier), never on an emotion/motion-cue the gate doesn't recognize"}
  :call_site
  {:what "functions/api/chat.js, a Cloudflare Pages Function -- never the browser"
   :why "net-babiniku deploys as a static site to Cloudflare Pages; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY must
        never reach client-shipped code. The Function holds the key as a Cloudflare secret
        (not yet provisioned -- see :consequences) and is the only place allowed to call
        api.anthropic.com"}
  :official_sdk
  {:what "@anthropic-ai/sdk, not raw HTTP against the Messages API"
   :why "the claude-api skill requires the official SDK whenever one exists for the project's
        language; Cloudflare Pages Functions (Workers runtime, fetch-based) are SDK-compatible
        -- no technical blocker forced raw HTTP here"}
  :persona_schema_source_of_truth
  {:what "babiniku.persona (new .cljc namespace) builds the system prompt + structured-output
          schema from a babiniku.character roster entry -- pure, bb-testable, no HTTP.
          functions/api/chat.js cannot run Clojure, so it carries a manual, DOCUMENTED mirror
          of the roster/persona/schema data"
   :precedent "same duplication call babiniku.vrm-bridge's own docstring already makes: a
              whole separate build pipeline isn't worth it for a handful of small, rarely-
              changed functions/data"
   :test_gate "bb persona is the source-of-truth test for the .cljc side; the JS mirror's top
              comment names exactly which .cljc files/tests it must stay in sync with"}
  :richer_persona_bios
  {:what "each roster character gained :persona-bio/:speech-examples (full backstory + voice
          examples, beyond the existing one-line :tagline)"
   :why "(a) improves in-character consistency, and (b) partly caching economics -- cache_
        control: ephemeral sits on the system-prompt block, and a terse prompt likely wouldn't
        clear Claude's minimum-cacheable-prefix floor, so the richer bio gives the cached
        system prompt enough length to actually be cache-eligible across repeated turns"}
  :honest_default
  {:what "if ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is unset, the Function returns 503 with an explicit 'not yet
          provisioned (準備中)' message -- never a crash, never a fabricated reply -- mirroring
          babiniku.monetization's UnprovisionedCapability pattern (ADR-0084 precedent)"
   :ui_side "babiniku.ui.events' :chat/error never appends a ledger entry for a failed fetch; a
            real turn only reaches the ledger by passing through babiniku.governor/review-turn
            via :governor/propose -- the same gate every pre-existing demo button used"}}

 :consequences
 {:api_key_not_provisioned "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not yet a Cloudflare Pages secret for
                            net-babiniku -- the feature is live in code and deployed, but
                            returns the honest 503 in production until the key is added
                            (follow-up, alongside the still-open babiniku.net DNS/1Password
                            items already tracked this session)"
  :real_reply_unverified "a real successful chat turn against a live key has NOT been verified
                          end-to-end -- only the request path (a deliberately invalid key
                          reaching a genuine 401 from api.anthropic.com) and every honest-
                          default/validation error path were verified. Verifying a real
                          successful reply is a follow-up once the key is provisioned"
  :content_rating_untouched "the still-open ADR-2607062200 content-rating decision (free SFW /
                            paid may-include-NSFW) is untouched -- this backend serves SFW
                            only. A follow-up ADR must decide, if/when the paid tier is
                            greenlit, whether to extend this hosted-Sonnet-5 backend or reuse
                            club-shinshi's self-fine-tune pipeline for that tier specifically"
  :new_deps "net-babiniku now depends on @anthropic-ai/sdk (npm) and has a Cloudflare Pages
            Functions build target (functions/api/) alongside its existing shadow-cljs static
            build"
  :manual_sync_surface "the roster/persona/schema duplication between src/babiniku/
                        {character,persona}.cljc and functions/api/chat.js is a manual-sync
                        surface (3 characters, 2 small enum sets) -- bb persona/bb governor are
                        the tests to run before changing either side"}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "self-fine-tune + self-host (club-shinshi's precedent)"
   :rejected_because "no NSFW content is in scope for this tier -- the operational complexity
                      (GPU hosting, fine-tune data pipeline) buys nothing over a hosted Claude
                      model with a good system prompt"}
  {:option "Claude Haiku 4.5"
   :rejected_because "considered as the cost/latency-optimal default; user chose Sonnet 5 for
                      better roleplay/persona consistency, judging the cost/latency premium
                      acceptable at this product's current scale"}
  {:option "raw HTTP against the Messages API instead of @anthropic-ai/sdk"
   :rejected_because "the claude-api skill requires the official SDK whenever one exists;
                      Cloudflare Pages Functions are SDK-compatible, no technical blocker
                      forced raw HTTP"}
  {:option "free-text dialogue parsing (regex/heuristics for emotion/motion-cue) instead of
            structured outputs"
   :rejected_because "structured outputs let the schema itself enforce babiniku.governor's
                      exact vocabulary, eliminating a whole class of unknown-emotion/motion-
                      cue HARD-holds caused by imprecise free-text instruction-following"}
  {:option "a shared build artifact (e.g. a shadow-cljs :node-library target) instead of a
            manually duplicated JS mirror of the persona/schema logic"
   :rejected_because "coupling the Cloudflare Functions build to the shadow-cljs pipeline for 3
                      small character records and two enum lists is more machinery than the
                      current scale justifies -- same reasoning babiniku.vrm-bridge's own
                      docstring already gives for its own small-glue duplication"}]}